{"reference":"Psalms 126","book":"Psalms","chapter":126,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Surrounding Collection","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One way of reading Psalm 126 is within the surrounding collection of Psalms 120–134, which includes Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. In this wider setting, communal psalms remember devastation and exile while also giving voice to return, thanksgiving, and praise. Psalm 126’s movement from remembered restoration to a plea for renewed restoration fits this larger pattern.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_126_e8bc9ea7684ca6de64f20dd7"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}